When you try to take a heavy item out of a bag or box, you often get
a message saying you can't carry that much.  This seems buggy.
If you could carry the bag with the spellbook in it in the first place,
you should be able to carry the bag with the spellbook taken out.

I once supposed that stuff in bags didn't count for weight (which
would make them really nice to have), but it's not the case.
Today I picked up a large box, but couldn't carry enough to take the
stuff out of it.  So I dropped the box and looted it - and then
picked up the box again!  I assume what's going on is that the
weight of a container includes the weight of all the objects in it,
but when you're trying to take an object out, the object's weight
doesn't get subtracted from the container until you've FINISHED
taking it out?  This is double-counting!

